</div></section>
<section class="section ferme ferme-page"><div class="conteneur">
  <header class="section-entete"><p class="surtitre">How we look after nature</p><h2>Ecology, every day</h2><p class="section-intro">It is not a selling point for us: it is simply how we look after the estate and keep it alive, from waste to water use.</p></header>
  <ul class="gestes gestes-grille">
    <li><svg class="picto" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-poule"/></svg><span><strong>The henhouse</strong>Leftovers (stale bread, fruit peelings, vegetable scraps) go to the estate's hens.</span></li>
    <li><svg class="picto" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-feuille"/></svg><span><strong>The compost</strong>Plant waste goes into two compost bins next to the henhouse.</span></li>
    <li><svg class="picto" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-bocal"/></svg><span><strong>Recycling</strong>Glass, plastic, metal and paper are sorted outside the campsite, along the track.</span></li>
    <li><svg class="picto" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-goutte"/></svg><span><strong>Water</strong>The drinking water is tested regularly by an approved laboratory. We ask everyone to use it sparingly, and washing cars is not allowed.</span></li>
  </ul>
